}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Takes the canonical minimum spanning tree (weight, then position, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), a minimum-weight perfect matching on its odd-degree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumWeightMatching"},{"type":"text","text":"), and an Eulerian circuit of their union by Hierholzer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the first vertex, shortcut to the first visit of each vertex. The matching is on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complete graph of the odd vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order (pairs i < j lexicographic), and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"circuit’s multigraph lists the tree edges by position, then the matched pairs in that order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the tour is determined. At most 3\/2 × the shortest tour when the weights satisfy the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"triangle inequality (not checked)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tours read the simple graph, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below three"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete; the sum along a tour fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":". When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FixedWidthInteger"},{"type":"text","text":", every non-loop edge’s weight satisfies n · (2 · |weight| + 1) ≤"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (the matching’s bound), checked as each weight is read, so a weight beyond it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps even on an edge the matching never sees; so n ≤ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (15 vertices for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int8"},{"type":"text","text":"), whatever the weights. An arbitrary-precision integer has no bound."}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n³): the matching on up to n vertices; the tree O(n²).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/Graph/christofidesTour(weight:)-6qvc8":{"title":"christofidesTour(weight:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/christofidesTour(weight:)-6qvc8","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Christofides’ tour (Christofides 1976; Serdyukov 1978)."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"christofidesTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind"